menu "PT Camera Configuration"

    config PT_MP_H264_FRAME_MODE
        bool "MP path: frame-mode H264 with temporal NDR (zero-copy bond)"
        default y
        help
            Run the MP (main path) ISP -> H264 pipeline in frame mode instead of
            flexa, and insert a project-local temporal NDR (3D noise reduction)
            bond before the encoder. The bond takes over the MP channel via
            bk_isp_camera_channel_acquire(), pumps frames zero-copy on its own
            thread, blends when ISO/motion gates allow, then feeds the frame
            encoder via bk_h264_encode_set_input(). When unset the project falls
            back to the stock flexa ISP->H264 bond.

    config PT_TRACKING
        bool "Enable pan-tilt face tracking"
        depends on TFLITE_MICRO
        depends on NPU
        select TFLM_FACE_DETECTION
        default y
        help
            Enable the face detection and PT motor tracking flow. When enabled,
            the tracking task owns camera startup and doorbell camera open/close
            skips the MIPI camera power operations.

endmenu
